Discard unreferenced sections from NSIS stubs and plugins

Every installer carries a stub, and the GCC-built stubs were ~117 KB
(x86) and ~133 KB (x64). Most of that is unused GUIDs: for
IID_IShellLinkW and IID_IPersistFile the stub pulls in two large
members of mingw-w64's libuuid.a, around 4,000 GUIDs and property keys
in all. Nearly all are selectany definitions in their own .rdata$NAME
sections, so -Wl,--gc-sections discards the unreferenced ones, bringing
stubs to ~51-53 KB on both architectures. Plugins get it too, for ~9 KB
total.

-ffunction-sections gains nothing in the stubs, which have almost no
dead code, and only adds per-function padding. On x64 it would also
leave a bogus zero-length .pdata entry for each function it removes.
On x86 it lets the plugins drop unused pluginapi helpers, ~20 KB over
all plugins. x64 plugins only grow, because the default linker script
keeps all .pdata, which references every function.

Do not add -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables. On x86 there are no unwind
tables anyway (SJLJ), and on x64 it strips the stubs of unwind data
while they still host plugin code and call back into it: a plugin's
catch around a callback, or an unhandled-exception filter, would no
longer be reached. Nor -fdata-sections: GCC's mingw section naming puts
zero-initialized objects in .data$NAME, turning the stubs' large .bss
buffers into file data, megabytes in the bzip2 stub.

---
 SCons/Config/gnu |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/SCons/Config/gnu
+++ b/SCons/Config/gnu
@@ -101,6 +101,7 @@
 
 if not defenv['DEBUG']:
 	stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Os'])                # optimize for size
+	stub_env.Append(LINKFLAGS = ['-Wl,--gc-sections']) # discard unreferenced sections
 stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Wall'])                # all warnings
 stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-xc'])                  # force compile as c
 stub_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-fno-strict-aliasing']) # not safe for strict aliasing
@@ -147,6 +148,9 @@
 
 if not defenv['DEBUG']:
 	plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Os'])              # optimize for size
+	plugin_env.Append(LINKFLAGS = ['-Wl,--gc-sections']) # discard unreferenced sections
+	if defenv['TARGET_ARCH'] == 'x86':                # amd64 .pdata keeps every function
+		plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-ffunction-sections']) # let gc drop unused functions
 plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-Wall'])              # level 3 warnings
 plugin_env.Append(CCFLAGS = ['-fno-strict-aliasing']) # not safe for strict aliasing
 
